The tests are failing because my test expectations were wrong. Looking at the code
:

```ts
for (const [res, amount] of Object.entries(cost) as [keyof Resources, number][]) {

  const repairCost = Math.ceil(amount / 2);
  resources[res] = Math.max(0, resources[res] - repairCost);
}
```

The code iterates through resources in order (wood, stone for farm). So:
- In the failing test "never takes resources below 0 when repairing farm (wood)":
 it has wood=4, stone=10. The repair cost is wood=8, stone=3. First it subtracts 
8 from wood (4-8=-4 -> 0), then it subtracts 3 from stone (10-3=7). So stone becomes
 7, not 10. My test expectation was wrong.

- In the failing test "never takes resources below 0 when repairing farm (stone)":
 it has wood=30, stone=2. Repair cost: wood=8, stone=3. First wood: 30-8=22, then
 stone: 2-3=-1 -> 0. So wood becomes 22, not 30. My test expectation was wrong.

